# Security Architecture Review

## Findings

### SEC-001: Path Traversal via Unsanitized User Input in File Read

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Severity** | **Critical** |
| **CWE** | [CWE-22: Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/22.html) |
| **Location** | Line 5 |
| **Confidence** | 99% |

**Evidence:**

```typescript
const content = readFileSync("/data/" + req.query.path, "utf-8");
```

`req.query.path` is user-controlled and directly concatenated into the file path argument of `readFileSync` with zero validation or sanitization. An attacker can supply `../../etc/passwd` (or any traversal sequence) to read arbitrary files on the server filesystem.

Example exploit: `GET /file?path=../../etc/shadow`

**Remediation:**

Resolve the path then verify it stays within the intended directory:

```typescript
import express from "express";
import { readFileSync } from "fs";
import path from "path";

const DATA_DIR = "/data";
const app = express();

app.get("/file", (req, res) => {
  const filePath = req.query.path;
  if (typeof filePath !== "string" || filePath.length === 0) {
    return res.status(400).send("Missing path parameter");
  }

  const resolved = path.resolve(DATA_DIR, filePath);
  if (!resolved.startsWith(DATA_DIR + path.sep)) {
    return res.status(403).send("Forbidden");
  }

  try {
    const content = readFileSync(resolved, "utf-8");
    res.send(content);
  } catch {
    res.status(404).send("Not found");
  }
});
```

---

### SEC-002: Missing Security Middleware (helmet, CORS)

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Severity** | **Medium** |
| **CWE** | [CWE-693: Protection Mechanism Failure](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/693.html) |
| **Location** | Lines 1–3 (application setup) |
| **Confidence** | 90% |

**Evidence:**

The entire Express application is defined in this file. There is no `helmet()`, no CORS configuration, and no other security middleware applied to `app`. The application serves file content directly to clients (line 6: `res.send(content)`) without any response-header hardening, meaning responses lack `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Strict-Transport-Security`, `Content-Security-Policy`, etc.

**Remediation:**

```typescript
import helmet from "helmet";

const app = express();
app.use(helmet());
```

