| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Rule ID** | SEC-001 |
| **Severity** | **Critical** |
| **CWE** | CWE-918 (Server-Side Request Forgery) |
| **Location** | Lines 4–6 |
| **Confidence** | 99% |

**Description:**

The `targetUrl` parameter on line 4 is taken directly from user input (`req.query.url`) and passed without any validation to `fetch(targetUrl)` on line 5. An attacker can supply arbitrary URLs, causing the server to make requests to:

- **Internal network services**: `http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/` (cloud metadata endpoints on AWS, GCP, Azure), `http://localhost:6379/` (Redis), `http://10.0.0.1/admin`
- **Internal-only DNS names**: `http://internal-db.corp.local/`
- **Non-HTTP schemes** (depending on the `fetch` implementation): `file:///etc/passwd`

The response body is then returned verbatim to the attacker on line 7 (`res.send(body)`), making this a full-read SSRF — the attacker sees the response content from internal resources.

**Evidence:**

```typescript
// Line 4: User-controlled input, no validation
const targetUrl = req.query.url as string;
// Line 5: Directly used in an outbound request
const response = await fetch(targetUrl);
// Lines 6-7: Response forwarded to attacker
const body = await response.text();
res.send(body);
```

**Remediation:**

Implement a strict allowlist of permitted domains/URL patterns, and validate the parsed URL's hostname resolves to a public IP address before making the request:

```typescript
import express from "express";
import { URL } from "url";
import dns from "dns/promises";
import { isIP } from "net";

const ALLOWED_HOSTS = new Set(["api.example.com", "cdn.example.com"]);

function isPrivateIP(ip: string): boolean {
  const parts = ip.split(".").map(Number);
  if (parts[0] === 10) return true;
  if (parts[0] === 172 && parts[1] >= 16 && parts[1] <= 31) return true;
  if (parts[0] === 192 && parts[1] === 168) return true;
  if (parts[0] === 127) return true;
  if (parts[0] === 169 && parts[1] === 254) return true;
  if (ip === "0.0.0.0" || ip === "::1" || ip === "::") return true;
  return false;
}

const app = express();

app.get("/proxy", async (req, res) => {
  const targetUrl = req.query.url as string;
  if (!targetUrl) return res.status(400).send("Missing url parameter");

  let parsed: URL;
  try {
    parsed = new URL(targetUrl);
  } catch {
    return res.status(400).send("Invalid URL");
  }

  // Enforce HTTPS only
  if (parsed.protocol !== "https:") {
    return res.status(400).send("Only HTTPS URLs are allowed");
  }

  // Allowlist check
  if (!ALLOWED_HOSTS.has(parsed.hostname)) {
    return res.status(403).send("Host not allowed");
  }

  // DNS resolution check to prevent DNS rebinding to private IPs
  const addresses = await dns.resolve4(parsed.hostname);
  if (addresses.some(isPrivateIP)) {
    return res.status(403).send("Resolved to a private IP");
  }

  const response = await fetch(parsed.toString());
  const body = await response.text();
  res.send(body);
});
```

