3. **Denial of Service** via entity expansion ("Billion Laughs" attack):
```xml
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE lolz [
  <!ENTITY lol "lol">
  <!ENTITY lol2 "&lol;&lol;&lol;&lol;&lol;&lol;&lol;&lol;&lol;&lol;">
  <!ENTITY lol3 "&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;&lol2;">
  <!-- ...exponential expansion... -->
]>
<root>&lol3;</root>
```

**Evidence:**

- **Line 8:** `DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance()` — factory created with defaults (external entities **enabled**).
- **Lines 9–10:** Comments in the code itself acknowledge the missing security features, confirming awareness that hardening is absent.
- **Line 11:** `factory.newDocumentBuilder()` — builder created from unhardened factory.
- **Line 12:** `builder.parse(new InputSource(new StringReader(xmlInput)))` — untrusted string input parsed directly.

**Remediation:**

```java
import javax.xml.XMLConstants;
import javax.xml.parsers.*;
import org.w3c.dom.Document;
import org.xml.sax.InputSource;
import java.io.*;

public class XmlProcessor {
    public Document parse(String xmlInput) throws Exception {
        DocumentBuilderFactory factory = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();

        // Disable external entities and DTDs to prevent XXE
        factory.setFeature(XMLConstants.FEATURE_SECURE_PROCESSING, true);
        factory.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true);
        factory.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-general-entities", false);
        factory.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-parameter-entities", false);
        factory.setAttribute(XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_DTD, "");
        factory.setAttribute(XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA, "");

        DocumentBuilder builder = factory.newDocumentBuilder();
        return builder.parse(new InputSource(new StringReader(xmlInput)));
    }
}
```

The most robust single defense is `disallow-doctype-decl = true`, which rejects any XML with a `<!DOCTYPE>` declaration, eliminating all DTD-based attack vectors. The additional flags provide defense-in-depth.

