**Description:**

The `deepMerge` function iterates over all keys of `source` using `for...in` (line 2) and recursively assigns them onto `target` without any key filtering. When called at line 15 as `deepMerge(appConfig, req.body)`, an attacker can supply a JSON body containing `__proto__`, `constructor`, or `prototype` keys to pollute the `Object.prototype` of the entire Node.js process.

**Concrete exploit payload:**

```json
